# Common Beginner Errors

### Error 1: Wrong file name

If you have:

```java
public class Hello
```

save the file as:

```text
Hello.java
```

### Error 2: Missing semicolon

Incorrect:

```java
System.out.println("Hello")
```

Correct:

```java
System.out.println("Hello");
```

### Error 3: Wrong capitalization

Java is **case-sensitive**.

This is correct:

```java
System.out.println("Hello");
```

This is incorrect:

```java
system.out.println("Hello");
```

### Error 4: Incorrect class name while running

If your class is:

```java
public class Hello
```

run:

```bash
java Hello
```

not:

```bash
java hello
```

